==================== Branch work275-vpair, patch #301 ====================

Add configuration option --with-powerpc-vector-pair-fp.

This patch adds a configuration option --with-powerpc-vector-pair-fp that
enables -mvector-pair-fp by default.

2026-11-17  Michael Meissner  <meissner@linux.ibm.com>

	* config.gcc (powerpc-*-*): Add support for a new configuration option:
	--with-powerpc-vector-pair-fp.
	* config/rs6000/rs6000.cc (rs6000_debug_reg_global): Print if
	-mvector-pair-fp is configured to be on by default.
	(rs6000_option_override_internal): Add support for the configuration
	option: --with-powerpc-vector-pair-fp.

==================== Branch work275-vpair, patch #300 ====================

Add -mvector-pair-fp

This is an experimental patch that adds an option (-mvector-pair-fp) that
generates vector pair load/stores during vectorization for float and double
operations.

